	)
	(text "Encoder A, B signal input to shift down a 5V encoders signal. Both the internal and external encoders share the same filter.\nThis was done for 3 main reasons:\n\n1. Prevent adding additional circuitry to prevent 3V3 pullup\n2. Have some protection in way of MCU\n3. (personal pref) Connector can be used for encoder pin debug"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 424.18 7.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "92fd2a4c-5942-4327-81f0-9a291ba1a20e")
	)
	(text "External Env Sensing\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 241.3 208.788 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
		)
		(uuid "938ff8a9-0813-4294-a9a2-c1d295fddc67")
	)
	(text "Setup here is mostly for if we have any type of sensing\n(strain gauge or haptic sensing) that is a passive \nboard."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 217.932 212.09 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9f120c42-4f86-4075-985d-23c9c493e57e")
	)
	(text "MCU SENSING"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 178.308 146.558 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a189867a-7536-4387-8b76-f2e3d5554cf1")
	)
	(text "USB"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 82.55 26.162 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a31fb2ef-a012-46e1-adca-7f4a50de7218")
	)
	(text "Magnetic Encoder is onboard, and is used when the esc is mounted behind a motor to read absolute position\nof the motor. It also provides A, B, and Z Signals, but absolute position will likely be preffered over\nthese signals. However, there is the option of using an external encoder, in which case the user \n!!MUST REMOVE THE RESISTORS CONNECTING TO THE ENCODER!!\n\nBoth an external and internal encoder cannot both be connected at the same time, otherwise the magnetic encoder \nmay be damaged\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 187.706 76.962 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "bab12590-dcf7-42dc-a49d-0c3362602fd9")
	)
	(text "10k at 25, \n3380K"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
